nce":[],"finding":"The plan states that under `src/` the only references to `parity_report` are 'its own definition and two internal reuses, container_fidelity_report and prerequisite_fidelity_report' — but two further callers exist: parity.parallel_run_and_diff (parity.py:302) and fidelity_spot_eval.py:194 (parity.parity_report directly).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6dc44e1df5798ba8","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Correcting an earlier claim in this plan'","norm_id":"nfb9091a65e6baa73","priority":0.22,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Reword to: 'under `src/` the references are its own definition, two internal reuses (container_fidelity_report, prerequisite_fidelity_report), the parallel_run_and_diff live driver, and the opt-in fidelity_spot_eval — none of them a production gate caller.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"insufficient"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The plan says errored ItemRecords are counted 'distinct from decision_flips', but it never pins the `decision` value an errored ItemRecord carries, and parity_report counts decision_flips over ALL gold pairs with no errored exclusion — so an errored v2 record (decision='dropped' per the precedent) paired against a block/advisory v1 record will silently register as a decision-level flip, contradicting the plan's own error-classification invariant and potentially failing a slot for a transient runtime error rather than marking it INVALID.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f935f3f1a7458449f","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Error classification' and 'Repeats'; scored against src/rebar/llm/parity.py:104-107 and fidelity_spot_eval.py:174","norm_id":"n56f15e99b426e891","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"State that errored items are filtered out of the paired lists fed to `parity_report` (recorded only in the classifier's own error-count fields), OR add an `errored`-exclusion to the flip computation, and give the errored `ItemRecord` a documented sentinel decision that the harness never pairs into the gold flip count.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The net-new error classifier's discrimination rule is under-specified: it must sort a sampling-parameter rejection (400 naming `temperature`), an auth refusal (AccessDeniedException) and a validation refusal (ValidationException) — but temperature rejections are THEMSELVES ValidationExceptions, and the plan neither states the classification precedence (temperature-check before the generic validation bucket) nor that the raised exception object/string must be captured for classification, while the precedent it copies (`_record`) discards the exception via a bare `except Exception`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1ff3d2614baa957f","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Error classification' and 'Step 1'; scored against fidelity_spot_eval.py:170 and bedrock error shapes in iam_s7.tf:26-28","norm_id":"n47e135c141f2be7f","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","scenarios":[],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Specify that each epoch's exception is captured (not swallowed) and classified by an ordered predicate: (1) message contains 'temperature' → sampling-parameter rejection; (2) AccessDeniedException / ValidationException → auth/validation refusal; (3) otherwise → generic errored — with counts kept in separate result fields.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_va